      <h2 class="lp-section-h2">Why Hinsdale Brick Demands <em>Expert Mortar Matching</em></h2>
      <div class="lp-two-col">
        <div class="lp-prose">
          <p>Hinsdale's estates and colonials built between the 1880s and 1940s used Chicago Common and hand-pressed face brick set in lime putty mortar. Using Portland cement on these homes today causes irreversible spalling — matching the original mortar composition is the difference between preservation and permanent damage. We serve zip codes {zipCodes} across DuPage County.</p>
          <p>Many Hinsdale properties sit within HOA jurisdictions or near landmark-designated areas, making mortar color and material compliance mandatory. All Masonry Services documents original mortar, uses historically appropriate lime-based mixes, and provides material specs for board review. Free estimates, written scope, no surprises.</p>
        </div>
